{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791569081,"nonce":"TPwQWmtQ9vme/9WKozPO8q/QIQE=","title":"Predicate patterns over _ and binders inside constructor arguments do not parse (Issue11157, TestMatch)","message":"`case CInt(_ \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 _ \u003c 12)` is an expression over `_` that matches when true; the RD parser stopped at `\u003e`. `case {expr: EConst(c = CString(_) | CInt(_))}` parsed as an object literal, so the binder was never a pattern. Or-patterns whose alternatives bind names fell back to the real matcher, which cannot bind through nested objects.","files":null}]}